    "Oral neprilysin inhibitors should not be used in combination with ACE inhibitors as they can lead to angioedema. A specific medication, omapatrilat, was associated with a higher risk of angioedema. Additionally, ARNi therapy should not be used within 36 hours of ACE inhibitor use due to similar risks. ARNi therapy was shown to have a numerically higher risk of angioedema in certain patients. ACE inhibitors can cause angioedema due to the breakdown of peptides like bradykinin and substance P. Beta blockers are recommended for patients with HFrEF to reduce mortality and hospitalizations. Treatments should begin at low doses to minimize cardiovascular risks and should be maintained long-term.": {
